{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-laplace","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical Laplace transform","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-adjoint-trace","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-heat-equation"],"tags":["hopf-algebra","grouplike","monoidal-functor","laplace"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLaplace","text":"categorical-laplace-transform.md","leanSource":"categorical-laplace-transform.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:categorical-laplace\"></a><p>The <strong>categorical Laplace transform</strong> is the monoidal functor</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{L}\\colon \\bigl(\\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A), \\ast_q\\bigr) \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\bigl(\\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A), \\cdot\\bigr)</code></pre>\n<p>defined by the Hopf pairing against the real exponential grouplike <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q(-s\\cdot) \\in G(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{L}[f](s) \\;=\\; \\mathrm{tr}_M\\bigl(\\exp_q(-s\\cdot)  \\cdot  f\\bigr).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.21.5","page":"b/def-categorical-laplace","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLaplace","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
